sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch04-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Early embryological data, up to and well beyond segmentation, are a subject for physiological and physical investigation, and their categories (yolk content, chromosome form and number, radial, bilateral or spiral cleavage) will only seldom and accidentally coincide with the natural or phylogenetic classification of the systematist.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Early embryological categories seldom coincide with phylogenetic classification";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter IV, “On the Internal Form and Structure of the Cell”; topic “Embryology and classification”. Scope: early embryonic development of animals"
}
